Cell["\<\
We need to make sure that the parameters we choose satisfy:
1. b n  = c 
2. c > 2\[Alpha]
3. b > \[Alpha] \[Eta]
4. \[Eta] in [b/c,1]
5. Efforts in [0,1]\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9059028815793037`*^9, 3.905902954779828*^9}, {
   3.918586183998045*^9, 3.9185862072041607`*^9}, {3.9185862480418253`*^9, 
   3.918586311828651*^9}, {3.918586570343376*^9, 3.918586579016672*^9}, 
   3.918586645043503*^9, {3.918597201586013*^9, 3.918597225315755*^9}, {
   3.920664674429929*^9, 3.920664679875753*^9}},
 FontFamily->"Courier",
 FontSize->13,
 FontWeight->"Regular",ExpressionUUID->"cc5c667c-2a53-4f50-8e5b-587eee82a370"],

Cell["\<\
Let us redefine the effort levels and indirect utility functions by \
substituting b = c/n, so we integrate the first constraint into the problem:\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.918778712976768*^9, 3.918778749458315*^9}, {
  3.9187789215394173`*^9, 3.918778926331369*^9}, {3.9187791041834173`*^9, 
